{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: close the cross-process configuration lost-update defect before the configuration-custody completion can be ratified.","body":{"branch":"request/config-cross-process-cas","conditions":"Treat config.json as one shared cross-process record, not per-Workspace memory. A Workspace opened before another process adds or repairs an actor must be able to advance its verified frontier without removing that actor. Independently opened workspaces that add or retire different actors must not overwrite each other's unrelated custody changes, and no stale writer may roll back a newer verified frontier. Serialize or compare-and-retry the full read/validate/mutate/atomic-save transaction across processes; fail closed if immutable identity fields differ. Keep actor keys and durable roster semantics unchanged, preserve AddActor/RetireActor rollback guarantees, and do not regenerate existing keys. Add deterministic tests using two independently opened Workspace instances for stale-frontier-vs-actor-add and actor-mutation-vs-actor-mutation, including failure rollback and a regression that reproduces the observed five-entry rewrite. Keep the kernel/application boundary unchanged or update docs/reference/architecture.md in the same head if its contract changes. Run gofmt, git diff --check, focused tests including race, go vet ./..., full go test ./... -count=1, and Windows compile. Publish exact-head artifacts and request independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review; the eventual merge must retire all live artifacts covering changed paths.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}